# Captured dumps are local working data, never repository content: a raw dump
# contains the capturing machine's public IP, harvested from WebRTC ICE
# candidates. For an anti-detect project, publishing that is the exact failure
# the project exists to prevent.
#
# To commit a reference baseline, redact it first and the name must say so:
#
#   cargo run -p fury-detect -- redact \\
#     baselines/chrome-150-macos-arm64.json \\
#     baselines/chrome-150-macos-arm64-redacted.json
#
# Even a redacted baseline still describes the capturing machine's GPU, screen
# and fonts — that is what makes it useful. Publish yours knowingly.
*.json
!*-redacted.json
